%% Sangati AI — Server Alert Flow
%% Mermaid sequence diagram: How a floor server receives and acts on alerts

sequenceDiagram
    participant V as Vision Pipeline
    participant R as Rules Engine
    participant RT as Alert Router
    participant P as Server Phone
    participant SRV as Floor Server

    Note over V,SRV: Zone A - Table idle 8+ min

    V->>R: Zone A state = IDLE, duration = 490s
    R->>R: rule_idle_table matches<br/>Check cooldown: OK<br/>Check dedup: OK<br/>Check fatigue: OK
    R->>RT: Alert generated:<br/>"Zone A: idle 8m, needs check"
    RT->>RT: Lookup zone_01 → assigned server
    RT->>P: WebSocket push to Server #35;1 device

    P->>SRV: 📳 Vibrate + chime<br/>Notification: "Zone A: idle 8m"

    alt Server taps ACK
        SRV->>P: Taps [ACK]
        P->>RT: ack action
        RT->>R: Cancel escalation timer
        Note over SRV: Server walks to Zone A
        SRV->>P: Taps [DONE] after attending table
        P->>RT: resolved action
        RT->>R: Clear dedup key
    else Server taps SNOOZE
        SRV->>P: Taps [SNOOZE 5m]
        P->>RT: snooze action
        RT->>R: Pause escalation 5 min
        Note over R: After 5 min, if zone still IDLE:
        R->>RT: Alert re-fires
        RT->>P: Push again to server
    else Server taps OVERRIDE
        SRV->>P: Taps [NOT VALID]
        P->>RT: override action
        RT->>R: Suppress zone 10 min<br/>Log as false positive
    else No response (90 seconds)
        Note over R: Escalation timer fires
        R->>RT: Escalate to Captain
        RT->>RT: Lookup captain for Zone A section
        RT->>P: Push to Captain device<br/>"⬆ Zone A: idle 10m — server no response"
    end
